Usage: od [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Dump files in octal and other formats.
Write an unambiguous representation of each FILE to standard output.
With no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.

OPTIONS:
  -A, --address-radix ARG  select output address radix
  -a                       select named character output
  -b                       select octal byte output
  -c                       select ASCII output
  -d                       select unsigned decimal 2-byte output
  -j, --skip-bytes ARG     skip bytes
  -N, --read-bytes ARG     limit bytes
  -o                       select octal 2-byte output
  -t, --format ARG         select output type
  -v, --output-duplicates  write all input data
  -w, --width[=ARG]        output bytes per line
  -x                       select hexadecimal 2-byte units
      --endian ARG         byte order for multi-byte input units
      --traditional        accept arguments in traditional form (e.g., od -x
                           file)
      --strings[=ARG]      output strings of at least BYTES graphic characters
  -S ARG                   output strings of at least BYTES graphic characters
  -f                       select floating-point output
  -i                       select signed decimal 2-byte output
  -l                       select signed decimal 4-byte output
  -s                       select signed decimal 2-byte output
      --help               display this help and exit
  -V, --version            output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
